![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In headless browser environments (especially under heavy load or when tabs are backgrounded/inactive), `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks might be throttled or not fire at all. Similarly, `document.fonts.ready` can occasionally hang if a font resource fails to load or gets stuck. Since `page.evaluate` does not have an internal timeout, these can cause the script to hang indefinitely.

Adding a fallback `setTimeout` for both `document.fonts.ready` and `requestAnimationFrame` ensures the script is robust and never hangs.

```javascript
async function waitForPageReady(page, timeout) {
  await page.waitForLoadState('load', { timeout });
  await page.evaluate(async () => {
    if (document.fonts?.ready) {
      await Promise.race([
        document.fonts.ready,
        new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 2000))
      ]);
    }
    await new Promise((resolve) => {
      let done = false;
      const cb = () => {
        if (!done) {
          done = true;
          resolve();
        }
      };
      requestAnimationFrame(cb);
      setTimeout(cb, 100);
    });
  });
}
```

