If `document.fonts.ready` rejects (which can happen if any font fails to load or is aborted, e.g., due to network issues or blocked third-party font providers), the `Promise.race` will reject. This unhandled rejection will bubble up and cause the entire script to crash with exit code 2, preventing any contrast analysis from running.

To make the readiness check robust, append a `.catch(() => {})` handler to `document.fonts.ready` so that font loading failures do not block the rest of the script.

```suggestion
      await Promise.race([
        document.fonts.ready.catch(() => {}),
        new Promise((resolve) => {
          timeoutId = setTimeout(resolve, 2000);
        }),
      ]);
```

