![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The hardcoded color `#b45309` has very poor contrast in dark mode (around 2.2:1 against dark backgrounds), violating WCAG accessibility guidelines. Additionally, inheriting the green background (`var(--success-bg)`) from `.notice` results in a confusing color combination for a warning notice.

Use the theme-aware variables `--notification-warning-bg` and `--notification-warning-fg` to ensure proper contrast and semantic coloring in both light and dark themes.

```suggestion
.warning-notice {
  background: var(--notification-warning-bg);
  border-color: var(--border-warning);
  color: var(--notification-warning-fg);
}
```

