![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

According to the W3C HTML ARIA specification, a `<form>` element should not be assigned `role="dialog"`. Overriding the implicit `form` role with `dialog` can cause assistive technologies (such as screen readers) to lose form landmark semantics or fail to navigate form controls correctly.

To maintain both standards compliance and the desired keyboard submission behavior, keep the outer `<section>` as the dialog container with `role="dialog"`, and nest a `<form>` inside it. Using `display: contents` on the `<form>` ensures that the existing CSS layout and flexbox/grid alignments of the modal are preserved without breaking.

```
      <section
        aria-label={title}
        aria-modal="true"
        className="vault-modal"
        role="dialog"
      >
        <form
          onSubmit={(event) => {
            event.preventDefault();
            if (canContinue) {
              continueFlow();
            }
          }}
          style={{ display: "contents" }}
        >

```

