body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If the owner process fails (e.g., due to a script timeout or execution error), it deletes the lock directory in its `finally` block without writing to the cache. In this scenario, the follower's `poll` function will repeatedly fail `statSync(lockDir)` and find no cache, causing it to busy-poll the disk every 25ms for the entire 30-second `lockStaleMs` duration (up to 1,200 redundant disk I/O operations).

To prevent this, we should limit the number of consecutive retries when the lock is missing. Since a cross-process rename gap is extremely brief (typically < 1ms), a limit of 4 retries (~100ms) is more than sufficient to handle transient gaps while safely aborting early if the owner has terminated.

```javascript
    try {
      if (now() >= deadline || now() - statSync(lockDir).mtimeMs > lockStaleMs) return;
      poll.retries = 0;
    } catch {
      // The owner may publish the cache and remove its lock between our cache
      // read and lock stat. Re-check once so that handoff still emits it.
      const finalCached = readGreetingCache(cacheFile);
      if (finalCached) {
        emitCachedGreeting(client, finalCached);
        return;
      }
      // A stale-lock contender may have renamed the old lock but not created
      // its replacement yet. Keep polling within the original safety bound.
      if (now() >= deadline) return;

      poll.retries = (poll.retries || 0) + 1;
      if (poll.retries > 4) return;
    }
```

